{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 48, :comments ["<b>And no uncircumcised person shall eat of it.</b> From here it follows that he circumcised them in Egypt, and on this our Rabbis of blessed memory said: He gave them the blood of the Paschal offering and the blood of circumcision, as it is said (Ezekiel 16:6): ״ואעבור עליך ואראך מתבוססת בדמיך״ — 'And I passed over you and saw you wallowing in your blood,' etc. Therefore Scripture immediately mentions: ״כי עשו כל בני ישראל״ — 'for all the children of Israel did' — as HaShem commanded Moses and Aaron; and the word כל includes that they were all circumcised and made the Paschal offering. And likewise it is written explicitly: ״כי מולים היו כל העם היוצאים״ — 'for all the people who went out were circumcised.' But earlier, in the commandment of the Paschal offering, it says ״ועשו בני ישראל״ — 'the children of Israel shall do' — without saying כל בני ישראל, because there were among them those who were ritually impure, and it is not possible to make the Paschal offering in impurity."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:58:21.463068118Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}